OL,2,Q/.!+.!/*%*%  /*%/*%+.!/$ CJONES IN - Qj
OL,3,Q5GOXFORD LOOK DOWN UNDER CWARD OUT   Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,COxford,Faiming for an 11th successive
OL,6,Fwin, are set to change their first-
OL,7,Fchoice crew less than three weeks
OL,8,Fbefore the race withCCambridge.
OL,10,FAustralian Graham Jones, 26, a world
OL,11,Fchampionship oarsman, has been called
OL,12,Fup for this weekend's Reading head of
OL,13,Fthe river race in place of Tony Ward,18
OL,15,FA member of the last three crews, Jones
OL,16,Foriginally declared himself unavailable
OL,17,Fbut can now spare time from his studies
OL,19,FCoach Dan Topolski said: "If it goes
OL,20,Fwell at Reading, Graham will be in for
OL,21,Fthe Boat Race."
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
